Small/Medium/Moderate/Large ADV raid complexes spawn in insurgency systems with these properties:
- per-size ship restrictions;
- capture timers of 10 or 15 minutes;
- per-site corruption/suppression contribution of 0.25/0.5/1.5/1%;
- Moderate sites grant a battlecruiser bonus;
- Large ADV is static with a 40-min respawn.
Mordu's Legion NPCs defend for pirates and pirate NPCs for empires.

dungeonInstanceCacheMgr.GetPirateInsurgencyIceHeistInstances lists heists. Spawn rules: only at corruption 3–4, with a 4h respawn that persists across downtime.

In the site:
- tanker NPCs spawn at the refinery and are web-immune;
- each side escorts them to its own scoring zone;
- the first side to 10 tankers wins 150,000 LP;
- pirates near the Upwell Thunderchild guards are destroyed.

A covert cyno:
- requires Cynosural Field Theory V and fits only covert-cloak-capable hulls (plus Etana/Prospect/Rabisu);
- uses 1/10 of normal cycle time and fuel (25 LO);
- is visible only to ships on grid;
- can be lit in cyno-jammed systems;
- can be jumped to or bridged only by Black Ops.

Industrial cynos:
- fit only on the Venture (50% LO role bonus), haulers, blockade runners and DSTs;
- use 800 LO per cycle base, 400 minimum with CFT V;
- appear on the overview;
- can be jumped to only by jump freighters, capital industrials and Black Ops; Rorqual and Black Ops may also bridge to them.

Show-info on a wormhole returns:
- destination class text (C1-3, C4-5, C6, High/Low/Null, Triglavian, Drifter, Thera);
- maximum ship size category (Small/Medium/Large/Extra large);
- reliable lifetime bucket (<1 day, <4 h, <1 h, expired);
- mass stability bucket (>50%, <50%, <10%).

All values are derived from live wormhole state.

A 10 s session change timer starts on any of:
- login, stargate/wormhole/jump bridge jump or jump drive use;
- dock or undock;
- fleet join or position change;
- ejecting, ship loss or podding, or boarding a ship;
- clone jump or clone swap;
- corp join or leave, or a corp wallet division change.

While it runs, further session-changing actions are refused or queued per the live error behaviour.

During the 60 s post-jump cloak (stargate or wormhole), the ship:
- is not visible on grid;
- takes no damage from bombs, smartbombs or ECM bursts;
- cannot be decloaked by proximity or bumped.

Any action ends the cloak.

Remote assistance:
- of suspects or outlaws is a suspect offence;
- of criminals is a criminal offence;
- that interferes in a war or limited engagement is criminal in high-sec and suspect in low-sec.

Command burst effects are filtered by the same legality in high-sec.

In low-sec:
- attacking a capsuleer ship (including with untargeted smartbombs) gives a suspect flag, not criminal;
- attacking a capsule gives a criminal flag;
- neither spawns CONCORD; sentry guns respond;
- jumping into high-sec within the 15 min criminal timer triggers CONCORD.

At security status −4.95 or below, a character is an outlaw:
- anyone may attack them anywhere without CONCORD response or penalty;
- remote assistance to them is a suspect offence, even for corp members;
- assisting outlaws in low-sec is not an offence.

Tethering is refused for:
- characters without docking rights;
- ships warp-disrupted below 0 WCS;
- ships with a weapons timer or with fighters launched and not abandoned;
- unpiloted ships (capsules tether immediately);
- structures without a quantum core, or in the abandoned state.

Tether breaks on:
- locking a target;
- launching fighters;
- leaving the 10 km-from-docking-ring range;
- activating a burst jammer, command burst, cyno, siege, triage or bastion module.

While tethered, smartbombs, bomb launchers and fleet ore compression are refused.

An abyssal filament admits one of:
- one T1/T2/navy/pirate cruiser, but no strategic cruisers;
- up to two destroyers, consuming 2 filaments (T3 destroyers allowed);
- up to three frigates, consuming 3 filaments.

Frigate and destroyer traces can be activated only by fleet members.

Filament activation is refused:
- within 1,000 km of a gate, station, mobile depot or another Abyssal Trace;
- inside a deadspace pocket;
- with an active capsuleer log-off timer;
- while post-warp invulnerable.

Each refusal uses the live error.

Inside an abyssal pocket:
- no warping in or out, no cloaking and no mobile depots;
- no Local channel; directional scan and map are disabled;
- probes outside the pocket boundary take damage;
- ships and capsules entering the boundary zone are destroyed.

At downtime, players in a pocket return to the origin system and drones in space are lost.
